Here is a quick-start setup guide you can add to your repository's README.md or send directly to someone setting up the project in VS Code.

Project Setup & Execution Guide
Prerequisites
Python 3.10+ installed on your system.

VS Code with the Python Extension installed.

Node.js / Chromium dependencies (handled automatically via Playwright setup below).

1. Clone & Open in VS Code
Open your terminal (or Command Prompt) and run:

Bash
# Clone the repository
git clone <YOUR_GITHUB_REPO_URL>

# Navigate into the project directory
cd report-generator
Open the project folder in VS Code:

Bash
code .
2. Set Up a Virtual Environment
Open the integrated terminal in VS Code (Ctrl + ~ or Cmd + ~) and create a Python virtual environment:

Windows (PowerShell / Command Prompt):

PowerShell
python -m venv venv
.\venv\Scripts\activate
macOS / Linux:

Bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
VS Code Tip: When prompted by VS Code with "We noticed a new virtual environment has been created. Do you want to select it for the workspace folder?", click Yes.

3. Install Required Dependencies
Install the core Python packages (pandas, openpyxl, jinja2, playwright):

Bash
pip install pandas openpyxl jinja2 playwright
If you have a requirements.txt file in your repository, you can run:

Bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
4. Install Playwright Browsers
Playwright requires Chromium to render the HTML template and export the PDF:

Bash
playwright install chromium
5. Verify Required Project Files
Ensure the following files are present in the root directory before running:

generator.py — The main generation script.

report-template.html — The HTML/Jinja template.

master-excel.xlsx — The donor database spreadsheet.

photos/ — Folder containing community_photo1.jpg and community_photo2.jpg.

6. Run the Generator
Run the generator script directly from the VS Code terminal:

Bash
python generator.py

Usage:

When prompted (Enter company/donor name (or type 'ALL'):), enter a donor name (e.g., NESTLE PANAMA) or type ALL to generate reports for every donor in the Excel file.

The generated PDFs will be saved directly in the project root as report-template_<DONOR_NAME>.pdf.